import os, sys

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
sys.path.insert(0, os.path.join(ROOT, "tools"))
import soundpass_gen as G

NOTE = '''0.6.3 (2026-10-24) = SAPLINGS FROM LEAVES + REPLANT FIXES, THE FARMING TREE = CROP FARMING, THE A1 ALTS = A LATE-GAME EITHER / OR
  (with SkyyClasses 0.1.49).
  1. SAPLINGS (research/Sapling-Fix-Trees-0.6.3.md; Skyy 2026-10-24: "trees arnt really dropping saplings right now"): every LEAF that falls
     with a felled natural tree (SkyySkills' skill:on:felled - it already passes them) rolls trees.leafSaplingPct (Server Setup -> Trees ->
     Abilities "Sapling chance per fallen leaf", 0-100 %, decimals, default 2.5; a missing line = the default, nothing rewritten) for ITS
     sapling - the leaf -> sapling table is made at BUILD time from Assets.zip (the sapling whose grown prefab holds the most of that leaf,
     else the same name; asserted: Oak -> Oak, Fir -> Spruce, Fir_Snow -> Spruce_Frozen, Goldentree -> Amber, Bottle -> Gumboab, Palm_Arid ->
     Palm; none for Burnt / Dead / Bramble / Autumn / Snow / Fir_Red / Rhododendron / *_Floor). Own island only when trees.replantWhere says
     so, never while the profile switches, given like every tree drop (TreeGather.giveItem: storage > hotbar > backpack; one "Tree bonus"
     line a feedbackMs). The 10 % per-tree roll and Replanter stay (they stack).
     REPLANT: a felled tree's pending replant is anchored to its FIRST log (radius 3; a log of the same fall within 1.5 s and 8 blocks joins
     it too - a wide crown never starts a second replant); a mid-trunk cut (a same-family trunk under the lowest felled log = a stump) plants
     the sapling on the first soil cell with air above among the 8 cells around the stump at its ground level (Skyy's default; was: no
     sapling); every skipped replant is counted by reason (stump / not soil / blocked / unloaded) in the server log line.
  2. FARMING TREE LEVEL = CROP FARMING (docs/answered/skills.md 2026-10-24 FARMING TREE LEVEL, popup -> "Crop Farming level (Recommended)"):
     farming.average defaults to false (Server Setup -> Trees "Farming tree uses the average" OFF) - the Farming tree's points = the crop
     Farming level. ONE-TIME UPDATE TreeMig063 (PROJECT-RULES 4, TreeMig052's machinery): only a line still holding the old default true
     moves to false; History first; one Undo-able change-log row; marker "Farming tree level (SkyyTrees 0.6.3)". Spent points stay; the
     new points are simply free (a tree with more spent than points keeps every rank - buying waits).
  3. THE A1 ALTS = LATE-GAME EITHER / OR (docs/answered/classes.md 2026-10-24 A1 ALTS): branch 1 of every class tree SPLITS into two PATHS
     (tools/trees_v3_data.py r063_apply: rows split..5 - the split is row 3, row 2 for Spellblade / Priest - path A on the left of each ring,
     path B on the right, the trunk in the middle); the two A1-alts are the free ability nodes at the END of their path (row 5, the OR pair).
     Buying any node of one path TAKES that path: the other path's nodes and its alt lock (map: Locked; panel: "you took the X path") until
     a respec of the class tree; there is no swap button any more (the alt is the path you took - SkyyClasses 0.1.49 follows it and refuses
     its old /cast switch). A few generic passives moved into branch 1's trunk so each path alone opens every row (R063_LEND). Respec and
     rebirth keep ability + modifier LEVELS (SkyyClasses' use counts are never touched); the unlocks are bought again - a rebirth now also
     ends the abilities kept from an older layout (Class.<C>.gf). tree:fn:abil gains ",v5" (the alt is a tree path).
     ONE-TIME UPDATE alt063 (PROJECT-RULES 4, the fold's machinery) per profile file: a verified History copy (history/alt063/<pkey>
     .properties) first; per class tree: the alt the player uses (SkyyClasses' pick when they had both alts - class:fn:migInfo; else the path
     they bought into) is KEPT (Class.<C>.gf, until a respec) with its levels, the other path's ranks are REFUNDED (points back), an A2 / A2-alt
     the moved passives would close stays theirs (gf); alt063=done; one Undo-able line per profile in alt-changes.log. Waits read-only (like
     the fold) while SkyyClasses cannot answer and a pick is needed.
  SAVED DATA: players/<pkey>.properties: the other path's rank lines go, Class.<C>.gf + alt063=done are written once; trees.properties:
  farming.average true -> false once (+ the marker line). ROLLBACK to 0.6.2: together with SkyyClasses 0.1.48; 0.6.2 shows the old
  layout again (both alts free at row 2 - the refunded ranks stay refunded; alt063 / gf lines are read as before); Undo the TreeMig063 row
  in Server Setup -> Changes first if the average should come back.
'''

P = G.Patch(os.path.join(ROOT, "SkyyTrees", "build_skyytrees_0.6.2.py"), os.path.join(ROOT, "SkyyTrees", "build_skyytrees_0.6.3.py"))
